## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | lib/src/session_repair.dart | 🚨 blocking fa session repair corrupts the session file when the fixed line shares a merged span with multi byte utf 8 content spantexttowrite splices gh 2178 line rewrites into a merged kept span using byte offsets as utf 16 code unit offsets on the decoded string dart final original utf8 decode bytes allowmalformed true code units buffer write original substring cursor span 1 key span 1 byte offsets final lineend original indexof n key span 1 byte offset cursor lineend 0 span 2 span 1 lineend 1 sessionscannedline start end are byte offsets session line scanner dart 36–47 and kept spans merge contiguous lines appendspan so any multi byte utf 8 content non ascii payload — normal in this project before the poison line inside the same merged span shifts every byte offset off the string positions verified by execution on this branch repro header a message with russian payload привет мир — длинная русская строка для многобайтности poison custom line a child message repairsessionledgers repaired file has unparseable lines type custom id poison 1 parentid m1 type custom id poison 1 parentid m1 ti… the splice cut mid record and concatenated two half lines — the repaired file replaces the live session file via the atomic swap the poison record becomes a permanently unreadable torn line gh 1073 conservatism keeps it verbatim on every future repair and only file bak remains recoverable the pr s own tests pass only because their fixtures are pure ascii byte offsets ≡ char offsets this is the sanctioned unbrick tool for exactly the incident s 664 mb russian language session — it must not mangle it fix sketch splice in byte space or per line — split the span s raw bytes on 0x0a list int indexof then per line emit either utf8 decode linebytes or linerewrites key replacement never mixing byte offsets into decoded string positions add a non ascii fixture to the repair test e g a cyrilic message line adjacent to the poison line |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/session/windowed_session_storage.dart | ⚠️ important the new cycle guard truncates legitimate branch walks — silent context loss when below window records exceed the resident set the rewritten guard bounds the walk by the resident count only dart var walked 0 while current null if current timestampdegraded path add current if walked entries length break ← entries excludes appendedbelow final parent byid parentid appendedbelow parentid but the walk itself traverses appendedbelow records leaf and parent lookups both fall through to it and those are not members of entries ingestbelowwindow indexes them without being indexed into the window same for the deep paged append path at windowed session storage dart 1198–1201 any legitimate branch longer than the resident set is silently cut verified by execution on this branch repro 650 record chain → jumptorecord m1 deep pages the window → a second process appends 250 records chained from the tail → ingestappended → getpathtoroot x250 expected origin main no guard 250 records actual 101 records — the oldest 149 ancestors of the live branch vanish from the path this is precisely the shared file scenario the incident describes a second fa process appending to the same jsonl while this instance is deep paged getpathtoroot feeds buildcontextmessages so the model silently loses the oldest context of the appended region — a regression that also violates the card s own reg 1 invariant zero behavior change for valid input note the sibling guard in jsonlsessionstorage getpathtoroot line 1914 is safe there entries holds every record and walked ≡ path length for valid input fix sketch bound by entries length appendedbelow length still finite admits every legitimate walk or carry a visited id set |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

